\begin{aligned}
d_1 &= \sqrt{2(19)^2} \\
d_2 &= \sqrt{2(17)^2}
\end{aligned}
\] Then the ratio of their areas is \[
\frac{(side_1)^2}{(side_2)^2} = \left(\frac{\sqrt{2(19)^2}}{\sqrt{2(17)^2}}\right)^2 = \frac{361}{578}.
\] The area difference is \[
\text{area}_1 - \text{area}_2 = (side_1)^2 - (side_2)^2 = 361 - 578 = -217.
\] Since area cannot be negative, let's take the absolute value. Thus, the area difference is $\boxed{217}$ square inches.

